# Jupyter notebooks: last-write-wins on merge conflicts.
#
# Rationale: notebooks here are analysis artefacts edited on one machine at
# a time. We don't want merge markers in JSON, and we accept silently
# dropping diverged edits in exchange for friction-free pulls.
#
# Requires a one-time per-clone git config on every machine that pulls
# this repo — without it, git falls back to the default merge and you'll
# see conflict markers in the .ipynb JSON:
#
#     git config --global merge.theirs.name "always take incoming"
#
#     # PowerShell / Windows:
#     git config --global merge.theirs.driver 'cmd /c copy /Y \"%B\" \"%A\"'
#
#     # bash / Linux / macOS:
#     git config --global merge.theirs.driver 'cp -f "%B" "%A"'
#
# %A is the current/ours file; %B is the incoming/theirs file. The driver
# copies %B over %A and exits 0 — git treats the conflict as resolved.

*.ipynb merge=theirs
